	quest.3400000000000010.quest_subtitle: "Primitive work starts with bad tools and patience. Crude hands still need edges, bindings, and something worth cutting. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.3400000000000010.title: "Crude Hands"
	quest.3400000000000015.quest_subtitle: "Fiber is primitive progress made visible. If you stop gathering it, half your recipes quietly stop existing. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.3400000000000015.title: "Plant Fiber Matters"
	quest.3400000000000018.quest_subtitle: "Wood only matters once you can actually work it. Primitive materials turn logs into shelter, tools, and useful shapes. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.3400000000000018.title: "Work the Wood"
	quest.340000000000001D.quest_subtitle: "Carry water first. The pack expects clean water and route planning before long wandering becomes normal. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.340000000000001D.title: "First Canteen Path"
	quest.3400000000000020.quest_subtitle: "Bad water is still a trap. Purification is not optional just because you found a river. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.3400000000000020.title: "Water That Won't Wreck You"
	quest.3400000000000023.quest_subtitle: "Heat purifies. A furnace is part of your water plan long before it becomes part of your metal plan. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.3400000000000023.title: "Boil Before Travel"
	quest.3400000000000026.quest_subtitle: "A safe canteen is what lets you stop fearing every hill as a one-way trip. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.3400000000000026.title: "Purified for the Road"
	quest.3400000000000037.quest_subtitle: "A shield, clean water, torches, and bandages are not adventure flavor. They are the minimum respect a ruin deserves. Primitive combat and exploration are both about control, exits, and returning with more knowledge than damage."
	quest.3400000000000037.title: "Scout's Pack"
	quest.340000000000003C.quest_subtitle: "Pick the small fight first. Primitive combat is a lesson in exits, not kill counts. Primitive combat and exploration are both about control, exits, and returning with more knowledge than damage."
	quest.340000000000003C.title: "Pick the Small Fight"
	quest.3400000000000041.quest_subtitle: "Torches, a path out, and one controlled retreat are more valuable than a loot chest you cannot survive claiming. Primitive combat and exploration are both about control, exits, and returning with more knowledge than damage."
	quest.3400000000000041.title: "Pathfinder's Tools"
	quest.3400000000000045.quest_subtitle: "Bones, leather, and a little confidence are enough. Your first combat branch is about not dying stupidly, not dominating. Primitive combat and exploration are both about control, exits, and returning with more knowledge than damage."
	quest.3400000000000045.title: "Hunter's Readiness"
	quest.3400000000000055.quest_subtitle: "Simple rotation is still work. The point is not to become industrial overnight, only to make one job hurt less. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.3400000000000055.title: "Simple Rotation"
	quest.3400000000000059.quest_subtitle: "The Engineer's Hammer belongs here because first works should still feel manual, weighted, and grounded. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.3400000000000059.title: "Hammer and Handwork"
	quest.340000000000005C.quest_subtitle: "A millstone is the right first machine because it makes old work easier without pretending the age is solved. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.340000000000005C.title: "First Machine Job"
	quest.340000000000005F.quest_subtitle: "Hand power is primitive logic extended, not abandoned. You are still the engine, just with better leverage. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.340000000000005F.title: "Hand Power First"
	quest.3400000000000065.quest_subtitle: "Primitive mastery begins with one honest realization: you are no longer waking up behind the world every morning. This is a structural milestone, meant to keep the progression readable now and expandable later without rewriting the whole book."
	quest.3400000000000065.title: "Established at Last"
	quest.3400000000000069.quest_subtitle: "You are established. Primitive survival is no longer an emergency, and the world can finally demand broader ambition. This is a structural milestone, meant to keep the progression readable now and expandable later without rewriting the whole book."
	quest.3400000000000069.title: "Beyond Desperation"
