	quest.3400000000000101.quest_subtitle: "Seasons and exposure matter because the world is not tuned to your convenience. Read the year before it punishes you. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.3400000000000101.title: "Read the Season"
	quest.3400000000000104.quest_subtitle: "A bad wound and a bad forecast can be the same problem if you insist on pushing forward anyway. Every minute of delay compounds the damage, so the goal here is to build a habit of stopping a problem before it becomes a retreat."
	quest.3400000000000104.title: "Patch Yourself Up"
	quest.3400000000000107.quest_subtitle: "The thermometer is not flavor. If you are traveling blind into cold or heat, you are just gambling with a slower death. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.3400000000000107.title: "Thermometer Sense"
	quest.3400000000000110.quest_subtitle: "A hot meal slows panic down. Primitive food is supposed to feel local, handmade, and never quite abundant. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000110.title: "Three Meals, Not One"
	quest.3400000000000116.quest_subtitle: "Wild food buys time. It does not solve hunger forever, but it keeps the next step possible. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000116.title: "Wild Garden"
	quest.340000000000011B.quest_subtitle: "Cooking turns scraps into meals and meals into stamina. The pack expects a camp kitchen long before it expects automation. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.340000000000011B.title: "Cook the Scraps"
	quest.340000000000011E.quest_subtitle: "One lucky stack of meat is not a plan. Nutrition in this pack rewards rotation, not repetition. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.340000000000011E.title: "Nutrition Is Rotation"
	quest.3400000000000121.quest_subtitle: "Better meals quietly depend on better hands. A poor tool chain makes every kitchen feel worse than it should. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000121.title: "Better Hands, Better Meals"
	quest.3400000000000124.quest_subtitle: "You now have meals worth stopping for. That does not make the world safe, but it does make home stronger than the road. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000124.title: "A Meal Worth Returning To"
	quest.3400000000000130.quest_subtitle: "Only leave home when home can refill what the road takes. Primitive travel begins with discipline, not confidence. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000130.title: "Leave with a Plan"
	quest.3400000000000136.quest_subtitle: "A real travel kit is food, treated water, first aid, and enough light to leave markers behind you. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000136.title: "Travel Kit"
	quest.340000000000013B.quest_subtitle: "You do not need a perfect map to travel well. Landmarks, vertical silhouettes, and return paths matter more at this stage. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.340000000000013B.title: "Read the Horizon"
	quest.340000000000013E.quest_subtitle: "A waystone is not just convenience. It changes what counts as a reasonable expedition. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.340000000000013E.title: "Find a Waystone"
	quest.3400000000000141.quest_subtitle: "You are no longer stumbling out of camp at random. You can leave, learn, and return with more than luck. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000141.title: "Leave and Return Alive"
	quest.3400000000000150.quest_subtitle: "A locked chest is not just extra loot. In this pack, it is a promise that preparedness matters. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000150.title: "First Locked Chest"
	quest.3400000000000154.quest_subtitle: "Common locks teach the rhythm. They are practice with consequences, not free treasure for clicking first. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000154.title: "Practice Locks"
	quest.3400000000000159.quest_subtitle: "A clue is better than luck because it tells you what kind of danger might actually be worth the walk. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000159.title: "Clues Beat Luck"
	quest.340000000000015C.quest_subtitle: "You are ready for more than practice locks now. The better ruins can start mattering without breaking Primitive progression. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.340000000000015C.title: "Treasure Tier Two"
	quest.3400000000000170.quest_subtitle: "A furnace becomes important because it feeds water, food, and eventually metal. Primitive advancement still starts with heat. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.3400000000000170.title: "Fired Necessity"
	quest.3400000000000173.quest_subtitle: "One iron ingot is less about power than proof. It means your camp can now turn patience into permanence. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.3400000000000173.title: "First Iron"
	quest.3400000000000176.quest_subtitle: "Your first durable tool should solve a real camp problem, not just announce that the age changed. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.3400000000000176.title: "Tool for the Job"
	quest.3400000000000179.quest_subtitle: "A better axe means a faster camp, better fuel, and less time exposed while gathering. Iron should feel useful immediately. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.3400000000000179.title: "Iron Cuts Better"
	quest.3400000000000181.quest_subtitle: "A working base stores, sorts, and resets you between trips. Primitive mastery begins long before iron if the camp is smart enough. A camp becomes a base when it stores, sorts, and resets you instead of simply sheltering you overnight."
	quest.3400000000000181.title: "A Base That Resets You"
	quest.3400000000000184.quest_subtitle: "Storage turns scavenging into planning. If every return trip ends with inventory chaos, the camp is still primitive in the wrong way. A camp becomes a base when it stores, sorts, and resets you instead of simply sheltering you overnight."
	quest.3400000000000184.title: "A Place for Everything"
	quest.3400000000000187.quest_subtitle: "A real work corner means tools stop living in your pockets. The camp should be teaching you where things belong. A camp becomes a base when it stores, sorts, and resets you instead of simply sheltering you overnight."
	quest.3400000000000187.title: "Work Corner"
	quest.3400000000000191.quest_subtitle: "A roof is not comfort fluff in this pack. If the cold, rain, and night can reach you, your camp is unfinished. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.3400000000000191.title: "Walls Against Weather"
	quest.3400000000000194.quest_subtitle: "Fire is not just cooking. It is warmth, drying, visibility, and the first thing that makes a miserable base feel livable. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.3400000000000194.title: "Fire Is Infrastructure"
	quest.3400000000000197.quest_subtitle: "Sleep matters once you can protect it. A bed is not a symbol of progress until you can actually wake up in one. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.3400000000000197.title: "Sleep Under Cover"
	quest.340000000000019A.quest_subtitle: "Warmth fades fast when your fuel plan is bad. Keeping a fire alive is a daily discipline, not a one-time craft. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.340000000000019A.title: "Fuel for the Night"
	quest.340000000000019D.quest_subtitle: "A sealed corner, a fire, and a bed change the way night feels. This is where desperation starts becoming routine. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.340000000000019D.title: "Warm Corner"
	quest.3400000000000204.quest_subtitle: "Smelt a glass bottle of water in a furnace. You'll create purified water, good enough for now. You'll be able to craft a canteen before too long, allowing further exploration. "
	quest.3400000000000204.title: "Clean Enough to Live"
	quest.3400000000000207.quest_subtitle: "Every fall, hit, and knock you take will lower your maximum health based on your limb damage. Bandages can help fix this, so always keep a few with you. Trust me, you won't feel overpowered for a while."
	quest.3400000000000207.title: "Stop the Bleeding"
	quest.340000000000020F.quest_subtitle: "Cold care is never just walls. Your shelter works better when your water, injuries, and exposure plan are not an afterthought. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.340000000000020F.title: "Weatherproof Habits"
	quest.3400000000000212.quest_subtitle: "The wind no longer owns your evenings. Heat that lasts is the first sign that you belong here more than the weather does. Comfort is not the goal yet; the real win is making weather stop dictating your schedule."
	quest.3400000000000212.title: "Heat That Holds"
	quest.3400000000000216.quest_subtitle: "Hide and leather are the first materials that start feeling trustworthy. They protect, bind, and travel well. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.3400000000000216.title: "Trust the Hide"
	quest.3400000000000219.quest_subtitle: "Clay is the first time dirt starts acting like equipment. Containers, bowls, and utility all begin here. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.3400000000000219.title: "Clay into Containers"
	quest.340000000000021C.quest_subtitle: "Primitive crafting is just smart binding. If the materials cannot hold together, nothing else in the camp will either. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.340000000000021C.title: "Bind It Tight"
	quest.340000000000021F.quest_subtitle: "Once you can reliably cut, bind, and shape what you find, the wilderness stops feeling like random debris and starts becoming stock. Primitive survival starts by turning scattered scraps into materials you can bind, shape, and rely on."
	quest.340000000000021F.title: "Hands That Can Make Things"
	quest.3400000000000223.quest_subtitle: "You are finally planning for travel instead of merely reacting to thirst. Exposure still wins careless fights, but not every one. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.3400000000000223.title: "Plan the Crossing"
	quest.3400000000000226.quest_subtitle: "Clean water, weather sense, and treated injuries let you leave home with a plan. That is late-Primitive strength. Treat water as a travel system, not a convenience, because distance is controlled by what you can safely carry."
	quest.3400000000000226.title: "Drink for the Road"
	quest.340000000000022A.quest_subtitle: "Food should start feeling stored, planned, and recoverable. If every missed meal is still a crisis, your base is not ready. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.340000000000022A.title: "Pantry, Not Pockets"
	quest.340000000000022D.quest_subtitle: "A little preserved food in reserve changes how far you dare to travel. Hunger becomes logistics instead of fear. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.340000000000022D.title: "Preserve the Spare"
	quest.3400000000000230.quest_subtitle: "The kitchen is where hardship starts becoming routine. Primitive comfort means you can feed yourself without improvising every evening. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000230.title: "Kitchen That Lasts"
	quest.3400000000000240.quest_subtitle: "Do not go underground hungry, cold, and improvising. Primitive exploration kills players who mistake movement for readiness. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000240.title: "Do Not Delve Hungry"
	quest.3400000000000243.quest_subtitle: "A route only matters if you can repeat it. Knowledge becomes progression when it survives more than one lucky trip. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000243.title: "Mark the Return"
	quest.3400000000000246.quest_subtitle: "If you can leave a structure with your gear, your supplies, and your route intact, that counts as real combat progress here. Primitive combat and exploration are both about control, exits, and returning with more knowledge than damage."
	quest.3400000000000246.title: "Leave With Loot"
	quest.3400000000000249.quest_subtitle: "You have been hit, learned, and walked back under your own power. Primitive combat is finally a tool instead of a panic button. Every minute of delay compounds the damage, so the goal here is to build a habit of stopping a problem before it becomes a retreat."
	quest.3400000000000249.title: "Bloodied, Not Broken"
	quest.340000000000024D.quest_subtitle: "A bed, food stores, and treated water in one reach turns your base into a recovery point instead of a stash. Every minute of delay compounds the damage, so the goal here is to build a habit of stopping a problem before it becomes a retreat."
	quest.340000000000024D.title: "Recovery Reach"
	quest.3400000000000250.quest_subtitle: "Primitive logistics are humble, but they matter. A home that saves steps saves mistakes too. A camp becomes a base when it stores, sorts, and resets you instead of simply sheltering you overnight."
	quest.3400000000000250.title: "Save the Steps"
	quest.3400000000000253.quest_subtitle: "The camp now works even when you are tired. That is the real difference between surviving in a place and living there. This step turns a single survival trick into a repeatable habit that the rest of Primitive can build on."
	quest.3400000000000253.title: "A Place That Works"
	quest.3400000000000257.quest_subtitle: "Iron without comfort is still a poor camp. The pack expects your first metal tools to rest on real stability, not replace it. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.3400000000000257.title: "Iron Without Comfort"
	quest.340000000000025A.quest_subtitle: "You are no longer merely scraping by. Durable tools, stable food, clean water, and a working home make the world feel answerable. Iron matters here because it shortens the work that was wasting daylight and making every trip feel more expensive than it should."
	quest.340000000000025A.title: "Iron Without Comfort Is Still Not Enough"
	quest.340000000000025E.quest_subtitle: "The first useful machine should feel intimate. One saved recipe, one easier task, one less reason to dread repetition. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.340000000000025E.title: "A Mill, Not a Factory"
	quest.3400000000000261.quest_subtitle: "This is still a hand-built world, but now it answers work with tools instead of only toil. One small machine is enough at this stage; the point is to remove one exhausting job, not to pretend the age is industrial."
	quest.3400000000000261.title: "Work, Not Factory"
	quest.3400000000000265.quest_subtitle: "Primitive treasure must never replace primitive struggle. The best early loot is guidance, supplies, and a stronger destination. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000265.title: "Common Treasure, Common Risk"
	quest.3400000000000268.quest_subtitle: "A better lead should point to a real place, not a generic reward. Exploration gets sharper when the hints get sharper. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000268.title: "The Better Lead"
