	]
	quest.34000000000003C1.quest_subtitle: "A hoe and a few seeds are the start of steadier food."
	quest.34000000000003C1.title: "First Farm"
	quest.34000000000003C5.quest_desc: [
		"Harvest sixteen &6Wheat&r from your fully grown crops. Wheat is the bedrock of bread, hay bales, and animal feed — the cereal that built civilizations."
		""
		"&aReplant immediately after each harvest&r to keep production rolling. Bone meal speeds growth if you're impatient."
	]
	quest.34000000000003C5.quest_subtitle: "More crop types give you better options when one season goes badly."
	quest.34000000000003C5.title: "Find More Crops"
	quest.34000000000003CD.quest_desc: [
		"Thirty-two &6Potatoes&r — a real harvest. Potatoes are caloric, easy to bulk up, and bake into baked potatoes that fill the hunger bar fast."
		""
		"Carrots and potatoes can be replanted directly without seeds, which makes them less labor-intensive than wheat once you have a starter stock."
	]
	quest.34000000000003CD.quest_subtitle: "A bigger harvest gives you room to plan ahead instead of scrambling."
	quest.34000000000003CD.title: "Seasonal Yield"
	quest.34000000000003D1.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fishing Rod&r unlocks the second food economy. Cast into water, wait for the bobber to dip, and reel in fish, junk, and the occasional treasure."
		""
		"Fish is a renewable food source that doesn't need farmland, which makes it valuable when your crops are still growing."
	]
	quest.34000000000003D1.quest_subtitle: "Fishing gives you a backup food line when crops are slow or the season shifts."
	quest.34000000000003D1.title: "Backup Food"
	quest.3400000000000511.quest_subtitle: "Tier two treasure is no longer a rumor. This branch begins when you start seeking guarded ruins on purpose. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000511.title: "Tier Two by Choice"
	quest.3400000000000515.quest_subtitle: "Important locks deserve better clues. The point is not more loot, it is better judgment about where to risk yourself. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000515.title: "Better Clues"
	quest.3400000000000519.quest_subtitle: "Rare vault rumors are for players who have both better routes and better tools. Primitive greed should still respect preparation. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000519.title: "Rare Vault Rumor"
	quest.340000000000051D.quest_subtitle: "By now the road is giving you fewer easy targets and more deliberate ones. That is the right moment for stronger treasure opportunities. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.340000000000051D.title: "Stronger Targets"
	quest.3400000000000521.quest_subtitle: "The next lock tier is not common, but it is finally real. You are now the sort of player the road can start testing harder. Treasure should reward preparation, because a lock is really a test of whether the route, the clue, and the risk were worth the walk."
	quest.3400000000000521.title: "Tier Three Opportunity"
	quest.3400000000000541.quest_subtitle: "Seasons do not announce themselves kindly. The calendar exists so you can prepare before the weather chooses for you. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.3400000000000541.title: "Season Watch"
	quest.3400000000000544.quest_subtitle: "Cold mornings and short days are survival problems long before they are aesthetic ones. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.3400000000000544.title: "Cold Comes Quietly"
	quest.3400000000000547.quest_subtitle: "Biome and season together decide how hostile a trip really is. Pack for both or expect a slower lesson. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.3400000000000547.title: "Dress for the Biome"
	quest.340000000000054A.quest_subtitle: "Reading the season before it reads you is one of the quiet skills that makes Primitive stop feeling unfair. The year is an enemy schedule, and Primitive gets easier once you start planning around it instead of reacting late."
	quest.340000000000054A.title: "Read the Year"
	quest.3400000000000561.quest_subtitle: "The river feeds players who can wait. Fishing is primitive security dressed up as stillness. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000561.title: "Cast a Quiet Line"
	quest.3400000000000564.quest_subtitle: "Fish are plain, dependable road food. Primitive travel improves when your food source is as calm as your route. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000564.title: "River Rations"
	quest.3400000000000567.quest_subtitle: "Aquaculture widens fishing later, but the early lesson is already here: easy protein and careful pace go together. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000567.title: "Aquaculture Curiosity"
	quest.340000000000056A.quest_subtitle: "Patience is a survival skill too. This branch exists for the players who learn the world by waiting instead of rushing. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.340000000000056A.title: "Angler's Patience"
	quest.3400000000000581.quest_subtitle: "Your home now survives bad weather, bad routes, and a bad day. It is a base, not a campsite. Food is not a reward in this pack; it is a stability system, and every improvement here should make the next day easier to survive."
	quest.3400000000000581.title: "Home That Holds"
	quest.3400000000000584.quest_subtitle: "You can finally pack for leaving instead of fleeing. That is the real difference between stability and desperation. Travel only works when home can support the trip and your route can support the return."
	quest.3400000000000584.title: "Pack for Leaving"
	quest.3400000000000587.quest_subtitle: "Primitive knowledge has become infrastructure now: stable shelter, safe water, real food, repeatable routes, and work that no longer feels desperate. A camp becomes a base when it stores, sorts, and resets you instead of simply sheltering you overnight."
	quest.3400000000000587.title: "Primitive Knowledge, Kept"
	quest.3400000000001113.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Campfire&r is your first heat source. Place one and stand near it to warm up — Cold Sweat punishes you for ignoring temperature, and a fire keeps you alive on cold nights."
		""
		"You can also cook up to four pieces of food on top by right-clicking with raw meat. No fuel needed."
	]
	quest.3400000000001113.quest_subtitle: "A campfire is your first safe heat source for cold nights and shelter setup."
	quest.3400000000001113.title: "Campfire"
	quest.3400000000001116.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Furnace&r smelts ores, cooks food, and turns sand into glass. Eight cobblestone in a ring around an empty crafting slot — you'll build dozens of these over a Minecraft career."
		""
		"&aPut fuel in the bottom slot, input on top, output appears on the right.&r Coal lasts longest, but planks and saplings work in a pinch."
	]
	quest.3400000000001116.quest_subtitle: "A furnace lets you smelt glass, cook food, and start making safe water."
	quest.3400000000001116.title: "Furnace"
	quest.3400000000001119.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Bed&r lets you skip the night and sets your spawn point. Three wool over three planks — the most important block in your starter base."
		""
		"&cMonsters will interrupt your sleep if they're within sixteen blocks,&r so wall off your sleeping area before bedding down."
	]
	quest.3400000000001119.quest_subtitle: "A bed gives your shelter a safe reset point and helps you stop roaming at night."
	quest.3400000000001119.title: "Bed"
	quest.340000000000111C.quest_desc: [
		"Two &6Chests&r — your storage starts here. Place chests adjacent to each other and they'll automatically combine into a double chest with twice the slots."
		""
		"&aLabel them mentally early.&r 'Food', 'Stone', 'Wood' — you'll thank yourself in twenty hours when you're not digging through a single chaos chest."
	]
	quest.340000000000111C.quest_subtitle: "A small indoor stash makes it easier to keep survival supplies together."
	quest.340000000000111C.title: "Chest"
	quest.340000000000111F.quest_desc: [
		"Sixteen &6Torches&r — light is life. Hostile mobs spawn in dark spots, so flooding your base and mining tunnels with torches is non-negotiable."
		""
		"&aOne stick and one coal makes four torches.&r Cheap, easy, and the difference between a peaceful night and a creeper at the door."
	]
