	quest.3400000000002D50.quest_subtitle: "The portal frame is built from Depthrock â€” the Undergarden's bedrock equivalent. Collect enough to lay the foundation before you use the Catalyst."
	quest.3400000000002D50.title: "Depthrock Frame"
	quest.3400000000002D53.quest_subtitle: "Step through. The Undergarden is not a dungeon. It is a complete biome system with its own stone, its own metal, its own hostiles, and its own rules. The Virulent Mix is one of them."
	quest.3400000000002D53.title: "Into the Undergarden"
	quest.3400000000002D56.quest_subtitle: "The Virulent Mix is the Undergarden's ambient fluid hazard. If you contract an Utheric Infection, find the cure before it becomes a problem. This biome rewards caution."
	quest.3400000000002D56.title: "Virulent Mix"
	quest.3400000000002D59.quest_subtitle: "Rotlings are the Undergarden's first dangerous hostile. They are not difficult alone, but they do not come alone. Kill one and understand the local threat baseline."
	quest.3400000000002D59.title: "Rotlings"
	quest.3400000000002D5C.quest_subtitle: "Froststeel is found in the Frostfields â€” the colder biome zone of the Undergarden. It is stronger than Cloggrum and represents the next step in the local material chain."
	quest.3400000000002D5C.title: "Froststeel"
	quest.3400000000002D5F.quest_subtitle: "The Depths biome sits at the floor of the Undergarden. The light changes. The hostiles change. The ores change. Going deeper is the point."
	quest.3400000000002D5F.title: "Into the Depths"
	quest.3400000000002D62.quest_subtitle: "Utherium grows deep in the Undergarden as crystals. It is the highest-tier Undergarden material and feeds the Infuser process."
	quest.3400000000002D62.title: "Utherium Crystal"
	quest.3400000000002D65.quest_subtitle: "The Infuser is the Undergarden's crafting station for advanced processes. Building one marks the transition from scavenging the dimension to actually working it."
	quest.3400000000002D65.title: "The Infuser"
	quest.3400000000002D68.quest_subtitle: "The Forgotten Guardian is the Undergarden's named boss encounter. It guards the Catacombs approach. Prepare accordingly before descending."
	quest.3400000000002D68.title: "Forgotten Guardian"
	quest.3400000000002D6B.quest_subtitle: "The Forgotten Guardian drops Forgotten Ingots â€” the apex material of the Undergarden tier. Use it to craft Forgotten-tier gear before entering the Catacombs."
	quest.3400000000002D6B.title: "Forgotten Ingot"
	quest.3400000000002D6E.quest_subtitle: "The Catacombs are the Undergarden's capstone structure â€” a maze of ancient stone, Stoneborn, and danger. Reaching them is the end of the campaign's main arc."
	quest.3400000000002D6E.title: "The Catacombs"
	quest.3400000000002D71.quest_subtitle: "Gardens of the Dead grows at the intersection of soul energy and dark soil. Collecting Soulblight Fungus marks the transition zone from Nether fringe to the Undergarden's deeper frontier."
	quest.3400000000002D71.title: "Soulblight Fungus"
	quest.3400000000002D74.quest_subtitle: "Soul Spores are a finer Gardens of the Dead material with light and decorative uses. Optional â€” this branch supports the Undergarden campaign rather than leading it."
	quest.3400000000002D74.title: "Soul Spore"
	quest.3400000000002D77.quest_subtitle: "Radgills live in Magnetic Caves â€” the deep overworld cave biome adjacent to the Undergarden's reach. A Radgill Roll is the practical first output of cave food preparation. Feed yourself well before going deeper."
	quest.3400000000002D77.title: "Radgill Roll"
	quest.3400000000002D7A.quest_subtitle: "The Chicxulub Enchilada uses Primordial Caves dinosaur ingredients. Deep cave cooking supports long Undergarden runs without carrying surface food. Optional but meaningful if you are spending real time down here."
	quest.3400000000002D7A.title: "Chicxulub Enchilada"
	quest.3400000000002D7D.quest_subtitle: "Dimensional rifts appear near areas of high planar stress â€” including the regions surrounding the Undergarden. Collect World Thread as acknowledgment that the rift hazard is real and active in these zones."
	quest.3400000000002D7D.title: "World Thread"
	quest.3400000000002D80.quest_subtitle: "The Rift Blade is a DimDoors weapon shaped from rift energy. Optional â€” useful if you are dealing with rift encounters while running the Undergarden approach corridors."
	quest.3400000000002D80.title: "Rift Blade"
	quest.3400000000002D83.quest_subtitle: "The Cave Tablets are Alex's Caves' field guide â€” a record of the dangerous overworld deep-cave biomes that border the Undergarden's approach. Read one. Know what you are walking next to."
	quest.3400000000002D83.title: "Cave Compendium"
	quest.3400000000002D86.quest_subtitle: "The Magnetron is the apex hostile of Magnetic Caves â€” a charged, dangerous encounter that marks your first real Alex's Caves boss milestone. The Magnetic Caves sit in the deep overworld layers adjacent to your Undergarden approach."
	quest.3400000000002D86.title: "Magnetron"
	quest.3400000000002D89.quest_subtitle: "The Luxtructosaurus is the Primordial Caves boss â€” an enormous bioluminescent predator that represents the hardest overworld deep-cave encounter in this tier. Killing it closes the Alex's Caves campaign beat."
	quest.3400000000002D89.title: "Luxtructosaurus"
	quest.3400000000002D8C.quest_subtitle: "The Watcher is Forlorn Hollows' apex hostile â€” a different kind of dangerous from the Magnetron. Forlorn Hollows and Magnetic Caves are parallel campaign tracks inside Alex's Caves. Complete one hostile capstone from each."
	quest.3400000000002D8C.title: "Watcher"
	quest.3400000000002D8F.quest_subtitle: "The Hullbreaker is the Abyssal Chasm's apex hostile â€” a massive deep-sea predator with no dedicated advancement. Kill one. It is dangerous, it is optional, and it is the honest ask for this biome."
